"With no other priest alive" sounds like that one isn't available
anymore.

> Not many more, especially if you have Magicbane.

The character is a chaotic (elven?) priestess, so not very likely to
have Magicbane, which is the guaranteed gift of wizards and normally
neutral - non-neutral deities will _never_ grant it if the character
is no wizard.

> >Now, if I enchant all my armours to +5, then I can get to -40 .  Would
> >it be worth my time and effort to do it?

No. Not _that_ much time and effort; -40 AC instead of -33 isn't that
much better. You could enchant your shirt some more, for -35 or -36.

> >Stranger the High Priestess  St:18 Dx:23 Co:16 In:16 Wi:24 Ch:18
> >Chaotic
> >Dlvl:2  $:0  HP:348(348) Pw:530(530) AC:-33 Xp:30/100011777 T:59446

Looks great. Getting this character killed wouldn't be a case of
insufficient preparation but of poor tactics. One thing that i find
very important to keep in mind on the way up is that the main
objective is reaching the correct altar. Leaving monsters behind,
running away, improvising on tooled horns, zapping things with
teleport wands and generally avoiding fights are all good technique;
when i'm _almost_ totally surrounded, the best move often is not to
fight but to use the breach and run off.

> >Now for the weapon:
> >blessed Rustproof +7 Frosty
> >Blessed Rustproof +7 Stormy

Stormbringer is quite useful - it weakens foes (by level draining) and
heals you; it's rather poor in Gehennom with the many non-drainables
there, but i find it well worth keeping for the planes.
Frost Brand is _very_ nice in Gehennom (esp. against demons), but many
monsters on Earth and Astral are immune.

> >Your life will be saved.
> 
> You have a serious hole in your defenses with the lack of reflection.

It's a nuisance, but not a totally deadly threat - with all the
resists, the problem with lack of reflection is the destruction of
wands and rings in inventory.

 Try
> to get a set of SDSM instead of GDSM, and obtain your magic resistance by
> some other method...CoMR,

That'd be a fair bit of switching around (including having to spend
quite a number of scrolls for enchanting the gear) that late in the
game. 

> or wishing for an inventory MR quest artifact
> like the PYEC.

Ermmm, that would require permanently converting to neutral alignment
(the character is a chaotic priestess), and wishing for an artefact
will have a substantial risk of wasting the wish by this stage.

> Either that, or dump the lifesaving amulet for an amulet of reflection.

That strikes me as the most reasonable option - except i'd suggest to
keep the amulet of life saving as a backup against foreseeable
non-instant deaths.

